# Profile two-column layout

`ProfilePage` uses a **fixed** `lg:grid-cols-2` story order. Do not auto-pack
or shuffle panels by height — that made the page unreadable. Columns may
stretch to equal height (`items-stretch`); content order must stay intentional.

## Required order

| Left | Right |
|------|--------|
| Identity | Experience |
| Addresses | Certifications |
| Education | Extra-curriculars |
| — | Links |

## When you add a panel

1. Personal / location / school → **left**, under Identity (Addresses stays
   directly under Identity). Education rows use a leading school logo mark
   (like Experience’s company logo) so the two stacks feel balanced.
2. Career / credentials / extras → **right**, under Experience in a sensible
   sequence (certs before extracurriculars before links).
3. Prefer this story over equalising column length. A taller right column is
   fine.

## Avoid

- Measure-and-pack / masonry that moves panels between columns
- Dumping every new section under Identity on the left
- Balancing Settings with this rule unless it shares the same panel pattern
